M('''# RoboGuide AI · Reproducible Final Project\n### ITAI 2377 | Domain-Specific AI Assistant | Tung Tung Tung Sahar\n\n**Team roster from the original plan:** José Tuozzo, Kim Nguyen, Huu Huynh.\n\n**This notebook is runnable on a CPU and does not connect to or control an actual PiDog.** It demonstrates evidence-grounded retrieval, version filtering, safe abstention, quality checks, feature engineering, baseline comparisons and evaluation.\n\n> Research integrity: the offline corpus consists of **24 curated summaries** of official manufacturer sources, not 24 downloaded full pages. The source manifest in the rows provides links, and the optional online importer collects fresh pages separately. The manual 43-question benchmark is a small illustrative assessment, not an external study.\n''')
C('''# Colab bootstrap: first open this notebook from the repository's GitHub path.\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport os,subprocess,sys\nif not Path('roboguide').exists():\n    if Path('/content').exists():\n        repo=Path('/content/Jose-Tuozzo-AI-Portfolio')\n        if not repo.exists():\n            subprocess.run(['git','clone','--depth','1','https://github.com/jtuozzo1616/Jose-Tuozzo-AI-Portfolio.git',str(repo)],check=True)\n        project=repo/'ITAI2377-RoboGuide'\n        if not project.exists():\n            raise FileNotFoundError('Project folder is not published yet. Upload RoboGuide-AI.zip to Colab and extract it.')\n        os.chdir(project)\n    else:\n        raise RuntimeError('Open the notebook from the RoboGuide-AI root directory.')\n# Uncomment next command when new Colab environment lacks dependencies:\n# %pip install -q -e '.[test,ui,online]'\nprint('Working directory:',Path.cwd())\n''')
M('''## 1 · Architectural contract\n\nThe original proposal requested a retrieval-augmented assistant with semantic retrieval, engineered metadata (version, entity, API, error fingerprint, authority), a confidence gate, citations and a CPU-only fallback. This implementation prioritizes a **reproducible, validated lexical/character hybrid retriever** on limited CPU resources; neural embeddings/FAISS remain planned work rather than falsely claiming their evaluation. It deliberately produces **extractive answers** so a generator cannot add undocumented commands.\n\nArchitecture: source-cited summaries → canonical schema → word/character TF-IDF index → 8 explicit features → version-aware hybrid ranker → evidence gate → cited extractive answer → benchmark + failure review.\n''')
C('''from roboguide import RoboGuide,error_fingerprint\nfrom roboguide.evaluation import load_benchmark,quality,run\nfrom roboguide.preprocessing import encode_features\nimport json,pandas as pd,numpy as np\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom IPython.display import display,Image\nassistant=RoboGuide()\nprint('Canonical records:',len(assistant.docs),'| Evaluation questions:',len(load_benchmark()))\nprint('Official-domain sources:',sorted({x['source_url'].split('/')[2] for x in assistant.docs}))\n''')
M('''## 2 · Source acquisition and preprocessing\n\nThe curated pilot is derived from the official PiDog FAQ, calibration guide, preset-actions API, PiDog repository and Robot HAT docs. Every row records an ID, title, version, subsystem, source URL, provenance label and content. `roboguide/ingest.py` can fetch **fresh official HTML** using an allowlist, SHA-256 source manifests, structural HTML cleaning, deduplication and chunking; it marks those chunks **unreviewed** until verified for hardware version and code fidelity. This notebook never quietly mixes the unreviewed corpus into evaluation.\n\nBelow, a deliberately corrupted *staging fixture* demonstrates duplicate removal, missing-value restoration from authoritative canonical records, boilerplate elimination and invalid metadata correction. Results measure our cleaning code, not errors in SunFounder's website.\n''')
C('''q,raw,processed=quality()\ndisplay(pd.DataFrame([{'Stage':k,**q[k]} for k in ('raw','processed')]))\ndisplay(pd.DataFrame(processed)[['id','title','subsystem','version','source_url','content']].head(6))\n''')
M('''## 3 · Mixed-data encoding and engineered features\n\nRetrieval pairs have **eight engineered numerical candidate features**: word similarity, character similarity, entity overlap, title-token overlap, API match, error-fingerprint match, hardware version compatibility and source authority. The categoricals (subsystem and hardware version) are one-hot encoded. Numerical scalers and category encoders fit **only on development candidates**, then transform the fixed test slice to prevent preprocessor leakage.\n''')
C('''table,transform,Xdev,Xtest=encode_features(assistant)\nprint('Development feature matrix:',Xdev.shape,'| test:',Xtest.shape)\nprint('Non-finite values:',np.count_nonzero(~np.isfinite(Xdev))+np.count_nonzero(~np.isfinite(Xtest)))\ndisplay(table[['subsystem','version','word_similarity','char_similarity','entity_overlap','title_overlap','version_compatibility','source_authority','relevant']].head(8))\n''')
C('''a='File "/home/user/pidog/test.py", line 22, in main\\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named robot_hat'\nb='File "/home/other/python.py", line 777, in main\\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named robot_hat'\nprint('Error fingerprint A:',error_fingerprint(a))\nprint('Error fingerprint B:',error_fingerprint(b))\nassert error_fingerprint(a)==error_fingerprint(b)\n''')
M('''## 4 · Core assistant: five+ meaningful interaction tests\n\nThe assistant first checks for unsafe or unrelated requests, uses a hardware-version filter, searches the canonical index, computes heuristic evidence strength and returns only content from cited summaries. **Evidence strength is not a calibrated confidence probability.** No model invokes shell commands or robotics APIs.\n''')
C('''examples=[\n('My PiDog wobbles after assembly',None),\n('My V2 zero button works but Python servo control does not','v2'),\n('How do I run ten push_up repetitions?',None),\n('The touch sensor has a HIGH reading',None),\n('Ultrasonic says -1',None),\n('Can Standard PiDog use Raspberry Pi 5?','standard'),\n('How do I bypass battery protection?',None)\n]\nfor question,ver in examples:\n    response=assistant.ask(question,version=ver)\n    print('\\nQUESTION:',question,'\\nSTATUS:',response.status,'EVIDENCE:',response.evidence_strength)\n    print(response.answer[:650])\n    print('SOURCES:',[(s['id'],s['url']) for s in response.references])\n''')
M('''## 5 · Evaluation: baselines, fixed split, feature attribution\n\nThe 43 manually written examples have a fixed 35/8 development/test partition. Retrieval is scored only for queries with a gold document; safety and status classification are scored on all queries. Baseline = word-level TF-IDF cosine ranking; hybrid = weighted word/char/metadata features. Metrics: Recall@3, MRR@5, status accuracy, intent accuracy and median latency.\n\nThe reported test slice is small, inspected during prototype iteration, and shares source-material origin with the corpus. It should not be presented as a blind external test. Evidence-groundedness and real PiDog task resolution have **not** been human scored. Permutation importance uses query-group separation and measures average-precision drop for an exploratory relevance classifier, not causal effects.\n''')
C('''metrics,interactions=run(save=True)\ndisplay(pd.DataFrame([{**{'Group':key},**metrics[key]} for key in ['development_baseline','development_hybrid','test_baseline','test_hybrid']]))\nprint('Candidate-level permutation importance:',metrics['feature_importance'])\nprint('Development MRR ablation delta:',metrics['development_mrr_drop_by_ablation'])\n''')
C('''for name in ['01_quality_before_after.png','02_baseline_vs_hybrid.png','03_feature_importance.png','04_corpus_lengths.png']:\n    print(name)\n    display(Image(filename=str(Path('docs/figures')/name),width=730))\n''')
M('''## 6 · Error analysis and risk review\n\n- **Success:** citations carry direct manufacturer URLs; wrong-version-only instructions are hard-filtered; no runtime paid API or GPU; the fallback is always available.\n- **Limitations:** curated small-domain corpus (24 records), no verified 80–150-page ingestion run, only 43 manually authored queries, no embedding/FAISS proof, and no measured clinical-like calibrated probabilities.\n- **Safety:** unsafe battery modifications are escalated; hypothetical repairs never execute; physical procedures should be checked in the current manual and with a supervisor.\n- **Next experiments:** run the online importer and verify code blocks; label 150–250 independent issue questions; run dedicated lexical vs MiniLM/FAISS ablation; calibrate abstention thresholds with a distinct validation set; evaluate citation correctness with blind human judges.\n''')
C('''rows=pd.read_csv('results/per_question_results.csv')\nerrors=rows[(rows['recall3']==0)|(rows['status_correct']==0)|(rows['intent_correct']==0)]\ndisplay(errors[['id','split','question','top3','pred_status','intent_expected','intent_pred']].head(16))\n''')
M('''## 7 · Collaboration and academic integrity\n\nThe midterm plan gave **José Tuozzo** pipeline integration and evaluation; **Kim Nguyen** data sourcing, preprocessing and quality; **Huu Huynh** retrieval, response generation, UI and testing. These are *assigned responsibilities*, not proof of implementation or of authorship of the original plan. The PDF and `docs/CONTRIBUTIONS_TEMPLATE.md` provide a verification form for each teammate to document completed tasks, diagram creation and references before final submission. Do not sign for someone else.\n\n## References\n1. [SunFounder PiDog documentation](https://docs.sunfounder.com/projects/pidog/en/latest/)\n2. [SunFounder PiDog FAQ](https://docs.sunfounder.com/projects/pidog/en/latest/faq.html)\n3. [SunFounder calibration instructions](https://docs.sunfounder.com/projects/pidog/en/latest/python/py_0_calibrate.html)\n4. [SunFounder preset action reference](https://docs.sunfounder.com/projects/pidog/en/latest/python/py_b6_preset_action.html)\n5. [SunFounder Robot HAT](https://docs.sunfounder.com/projects/robot-hat/en/latest/)\n6. [SunFounder PiDog GitHub](https://github.com/sunfounder/pidog)\n\n*End of notebook — output is reproducible with `python -m roboguide.evaluation` and `python -m pytest -q`.*\n''')
